[{:db/id "q-331954/field-1/d472470bf61b62667bf520b42074414f07d1266def1002f8f8325fe27d872b2d" :answer/id #uuid "f0b615d0-81b8-5c45-b243-fae76c4c682f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "39" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-331954/field-1/a4c8bdda186d0d425e9963bf17967cd5e356d934f319fa58135b8f8cf8a589f8" :answer/id #uuid "eb19f87d-1e4d-5313-ae6f-2ecb7fa8b53a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "30" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-331954/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "46a10090-99e8-5dbe-8438-8f682dc56fe8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-331954/field-1/d472470bf61b62667bf520b42074414f07d1266def1002f8f8325fe27d872b2d" :answer-field/choices ["q-331954/field-1/d472470bf61b62667bf520b42074414f07d1266def1002f8f8325fe27d872b2d" "q-331954/field-1/a4c8bdda186d0d425e9963bf17967cd5e356d934f319fa58135b8f8cf8a589f8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-331954" :question/id #uuid "98a70c61-b70c-50f6-869d-66013f377908" :question/math-academy-id "q-331954" :question/problem "Consider the following trigonometric equation: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x-{45}^{∘})=\\frac{1}{2}\n$$\n\n  \n\nThe general solution of this equation can be expressed as\n\n$$\nx={15}^{∘}+{72}^{∘}\\cdot n,\\,x=b+{72}^{∘}\\cdot n,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is any integer. Find a possible value of $b$ in the range $[{0}^{∘},{72}^{∘}).$\n\n$b=$\n{{field-1}}${}^{∘}$" :question/worked-solution "The general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x-{45}^{∘} & ={30}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n, & \\, & \\, & 5x-{45}^{∘} & ={150}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the two equations above for $x,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x & ={30}^{∘}+{45}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n & \\, & \\, & 5x & ={150}^{∘}+{45}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n \\\\ 5x & ={75}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n & \\, & \\, & 5x & ={195}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n \\\\ x & ={15}^{∘}+{72}^{∘}\\cdot n & \\, & \\, & x & ={39}^{∘}+{72}^{∘}\\cdot n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that $b={39}^{∘}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-331954/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fc8166bb-3a9d-5808-af53-a18ca99920f8"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-331954"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-16252/selection/3bf22c40d10f349d2917ff5137a2efa19cdb5e9f44ebf3e56ac31febb8aab17e" :answer/id #uuid "07a7fb6d-1b22-52ba-8f3f-0daeae266d17" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-{165}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-16252/selection/0dedc37c1c07b1d3afccefbc2cd1d676db0a66a60d8f6fa588da436c9c06df07" :answer/id #uuid "74ceac17-f52a-5863-a5bc-044723ffc88a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-{45}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-16252/selection/8fc7193c5b8057737764c1e1eb4c30dc73f3726403a2152ed72c83e00dbba4ca" :answer/id #uuid "914ab5c3-d6c3-5b42-a5ca-0d4df6aba908" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-{105}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-16252/selection/7213d14d95c3658d7bb915c9229b38965cc6bce1bf5b2c92ebf9cfed476f5100" :answer/id #uuid "9c2d6eb0-cfd4-5363-bf0f-0efb712803f0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-{35}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-16252/selection/9d601ae465622011eb1f48c4892bde7a595aea6aba63adf96700f41bf81ddb17" :answer/id #uuid "2302743b-5b29-596b-b8db-d3a6329ac0b1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-{55}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-16252/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "f9a4cb5c-fa4e-589c-b04a-84cce117001e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-16252/selection/9d601ae465622011eb1f48c4892bde7a595aea6aba63adf96700f41bf81ddb17" :answer-field/choices ["q-16252/selection/3bf22c40d10f349d2917ff5137a2efa19cdb5e9f44ebf3e56ac31febb8aab17e" "q-16252/selection/0dedc37c1c07b1d3afccefbc2cd1d676db0a66a60d8f6fa588da436c9c06df07" "q-16252/selection/8fc7193c5b8057737764c1e1eb4c30dc73f3726403a2152ed72c83e00dbba4ca" "q-16252/selection/7213d14d95c3658d7bb915c9229b38965cc6bce1bf5b2c92ebf9cfed476f5100" "q-16252/selection/9d601ae465622011eb1f48c4892bde7a595aea6aba63adf96700f41bf81ddb17"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-16252" :question/id #uuid "d9654a1b-7cb1-5764-826b-bc9327f43dc2" :question/math-academy-id "q-16252" :question/problem "Consider the following trigonometric equation: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x+{30}^{∘})=-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\n$$\n\n  \n\nThe general solution of this equation can be expressed as\n\n$$\nx=-{25}^{∘}+{120}^{∘}n,\\,x=b+{120}^{∘}n,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is any integer. Which of the following could be the value of $b?$" :question/worked-solution "The general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x+{30}^{∘} & =-{45}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}n, & \\, & \\, & 3x+{30}^{∘} & =-{135}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}n.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the two equations above for $x,$ we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x & =-{30}^{∘}-{45}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}n & \\, & \\, & 3x & =-{30}^{∘}-{135}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}n \\\\ 3x & =-{75}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}n & \\, & \\, & 3x & =-{165}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}n \\\\ x & =-{25}^{∘}+{120}^{∘}n & \\, & \\, & x & =-{55}^{∘}+{120}^{∘}n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that $b=-{55}^{∘}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-16252/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fc8166bb-3a9d-5808-af53-a18ca99920f8"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-16252"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-65848/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "3f40e1f4-6d41-59f8-bf01-021e79ceab9c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-65848/selection/9e11fa4df3725c69efaf2fb0a82d90e47a4519d002f721e23606c3d6290fb02c" :answer/id #uuid "1c2ea7f8-8be8-55d5-8f36-4a20fd925067" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-65848/selection/d027d90726f5bdbf1525aade1b6bde5c85e2082f2b792dfacee399fcc90e9833" :answer/id #uuid "a5a47d39-0b41-5176-af76-af7ca7749ddc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-65848/selection/21bc1f5ac2b6db8ca11973d9b85c1eeb6af2cd920b556e0cf3d98ab9a728286a" :answer/id #uuid "e0e3c71f-a4eb-5697-9a02-b66d9f85421c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-65848/selection/523b37883474afade764165f552bc128b7640323ff7244275508d19e6f99b277" :answer/id #uuid "537d4e14-d95d-53db-a43d-2601816e536c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-65848/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a4f91f24-660b-5989-8461-574ba0cf2e00" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-65848/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer-field/choices ["q-65848/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" "q-65848/selection/9e11fa4df3725c69efaf2fb0a82d90e47a4519d002f721e23606c3d6290fb02c" "q-65848/selection/d027d90726f5bdbf1525aade1b6bde5c85e2082f2b792dfacee399fcc90e9833" "q-65848/selection/21bc1f5ac2b6db8ca11973d9b85c1eeb6af2cd920b556e0cf3d98ab9a728286a" "q-65848/selection/523b37883474afade764165f552bc128b7640323ff7244275508d19e6f99b277"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-65848" :question/id #uuid "10102690-223d-5bcf-a385-350cb050888e" :question/math-academy-id "q-65848" :question/problem "Consider the following trigonometric equation: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{6})=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\n$$\n\n  \n\nThe general solution of this equation can be expressed as\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{\\pi }{6}+2n\\pi ,\\,x=b\\pi +2n\\pi ,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is any integer. Which of the following could be the value of $b?$" :question/worked-solution "The general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+\\frac{\\pi }{6} & =\\frac{\\pi }{3}+2n\\pi , & \\, & \\, & x+\\frac{\\pi }{6} & =\\frac{2\\pi }{3}+2\\pi n.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the two equations above for $x,$ we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =-\\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\frac{\\pi }{3}+2n\\pi  & \\, & \\, & x & =-\\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\frac{2\\pi }{3}+2\\pi n \\\\ x & =\\frac{\\pi }{6}+2n\\pi  & \\, & \\, & x & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}+2n\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that $b=\\frac{1}{2}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-65848/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fc8166bb-3a9d-5808-af53-a18ca99920f8"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-65848"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-274647/field-1/c087f5dc559272d193745a4428553203b94404f681d8529e6e619348c0528d10" :answer/id #uuid "0706ddf7-1823-5bc2-ab3f-bf282c0c2abc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-274647/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "1ae08936-817a-5f84-b398-1a2d05fa013f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-274647/field-1/c087f5dc559272d193745a4428553203b94404f681d8529e6e619348c0528d10" :answer-field/choices ["q-274647/field-1/c087f5dc559272d193745a4428553203b94404f681d8529e6e619348c0528d10"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-274647" :question/id #uuid "66dce54a-8cfe-5e60-a256-10588f9ab244" :question/math-academy-id "q-274647" :question/problem "Consider the following trigonometric equation: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{4})=-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\n$$\n\n  \n\nThe general solution of this equation can be expressed as\n\n$$\nx=\\pi +2\\pi n,\\,x=b\\pi +2\\pi n,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is any integer. Find a possible value of $b$ in the range $[0,2).$\n\n$b=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+\\frac{\\pi }{4} & =\\frac{5\\pi }{4}+2\\pi n, & \\, & \\, & x+\\frac{\\pi }{4} & =\\frac{7\\pi }{4}+2\\pi n.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the two equations above for $x,$ we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{5\\pi }{4}-\\frac{\\pi }{4}+2\\pi n & \\, & \\, & x & =\\frac{7\\pi }{4}-\\frac{\\pi }{4}+2\\pi n \\\\ x & =\\frac{4\\pi }{4}+2\\pi n & \\, & \\, & x & =\\frac{6\\pi }{4}+2\\pi n \\\\ x & =\\pi +2\\pi n & \\, & \\, & x & =\\frac{3\\pi }{2}+2\\pi n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that $b=\\frac{3}{2}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-274647/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fc8166bb-3a9d-5808-af53-a18ca99920f8"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-274647"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-327876/field-1/c89a78e01f135d27857f87b29786d3bde75753fd31e9ec00c0c39b58d64c0b12" :answer/id #uuid "75185d75-f5d4-5ffb-9d27-aba442321528" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "135" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-327876/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "c3f10820-c2b3-54b6-9b01-4fc2a979bbae" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-327876/field-1/c89a78e01f135d27857f87b29786d3bde75753fd31e9ec00c0c39b58d64c0b12" :answer-field/choices ["q-327876/field-1/c89a78e01f135d27857f87b29786d3bde75753fd31e9ec00c0c39b58d64c0b12"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-327876" :question/id #uuid "b3cf854f-327f-5c34-bbfc-5fd91da61753" :question/math-academy-id "q-327876" :question/problem "Consider the following trigonometric equation: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x-{60}^{∘})=-\\frac{1}{2}\n$$\n\n  \n\nThe general solution of this equation can be expressed as\n\n$$\nx=b+{180}^{∘}\\cdot n,\\,x={195}^{∘}+{180}^{∘}\\cdot n,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is any integer. Find a possible value of $b$ in the range $[{0}^{∘},{180}^{∘}).$\n\n$b=$\n{{field-1}}${}^{∘}$" :question/worked-solution "The general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-{60}^{∘} & ={210}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n, & \\, & \\, & 2x-{60}^{∘} & ={330}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the two equations above for $x,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x & ={210}^{∘}+{60}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n & \\, & \\, & 2x & ={330}^{∘}+{60}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n \\\\ 2x & ={270}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n & \\, & \\, & 2x & ={390}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n \\\\ x & ={135}^{∘}+{180}^{∘}\\cdot n & \\, & \\, & x & ={195}^{∘}+{180}^{∘}\\cdot n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that $b={135}^{∘}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-327876/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fc8166bb-3a9d-5808-af53-a18ca99920f8"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-327876"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-328241/field-1/a59e10e9ca0b8a69d2b8425f1c9930ee0733ea061a1d6430398562813d750649" :answer/id #uuid "1da1f529-a671-555a-85cc-177b012525e2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "120" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-328241/field-1/23a7b929cccc5bdeb88db3bdc770afbaf59570d63e930fc5c94f26cb6f5091dc" :answer/id #uuid "a17142ab-c730-52e5-8620-e381e5845f4c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "60" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-328241/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "e06ffba9-32a2-5216-b5d7-09ac7ed767e3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-328241/field-1/a59e10e9ca0b8a69d2b8425f1c9930ee0733ea061a1d6430398562813d750649" :answer-field/choices ["q-328241/field-1/a59e10e9ca0b8a69d2b8425f1c9930ee0733ea061a1d6430398562813d750649" "q-328241/field-1/23a7b929cccc5bdeb88db3bdc770afbaf59570d63e930fc5c94f26cb6f5091dc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-328241" :question/id #uuid "c742ee53-0710-5915-b4de-a43b4cebec18" :question/math-academy-id "q-328241" :question/problem "Consider the following trigonometric equation: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}+{150}^{∘})=-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\n$$\n\n  \n\nThe general solution of this equation can be expressed as\n\n$$\nx={720}^{∘}\\cdot n,\\,x=a+{720}^{∘}\\cdot n,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is any integer. Find a possible value of $a$ in the range $[{0}^{∘},{180}^{∘}).$\n\n$a=$\n{{field-1}}${}^{∘}$" :question/worked-solution "The general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{2}+{150}^{∘} & ={150}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n, & \\, & \\, & \\frac{x}{2}+{150}^{∘} & ={210}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the two equations above for $x,$ we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{2} & ={150}^{∘}-{150}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n & \\, & \\, & \\frac{x}{2} & ={210}^{∘}-{150}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n \\\\ \\frac{x}{2} & ={360}^{∘}\\cdot n & \\, & \\, & \\frac{x}{2} & ={60}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n \\\\ x & ={720}^{∘}\\cdot n & \\, & \\, & x & ={120}^{∘}+{720}^{∘}\\cdot n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that $a={120}^{∘}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-328241/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a180dc90-c6b9-577e-9eef-ed60ecafe4e5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-328241"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-330218/field-1/e8fca892866a06a1ab302627b9de911942e4dfff7666b327843df0729f3939b1" :answer/id #uuid "cc05165d-ad81-500b-b846-1dc45f03a177" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "105" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-330218/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "40693c9f-68a2-5c18-9307-28072c764274" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-330218/field-1/e8fca892866a06a1ab302627b9de911942e4dfff7666b327843df0729f3939b1" :answer-field/choices ["q-330218/field-1/e8fca892866a06a1ab302627b9de911942e4dfff7666b327843df0729f3939b1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-330218" :question/id #uuid "f8fdd777-5df8-5c21-87ef-46d12c5520f5" :question/math-academy-id "q-330218" :question/problem "Consider the following trigonometric equation: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+{120}^{∘})=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\n$$\n\n  \n\nThe general solution of this equation can be expressed as\n\n$$\nx=-{45}^{∘}+{180}^{∘}\\cdot n,\\,x=a+{180}^{∘}\\cdot n,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is any integer. Find a possible value of $a$ in the range $[{0}^{∘},{180}^{∘}).$\n\n$a=$\n{{field-1}}${}^{∘}$" :question/worked-solution "The general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+{120}^{∘} & ={30}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n, & \\, & \\, & 2x+{120}^{∘} & ={330}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the two equations above for $x,$ we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x & ={30}^{∘}-{120}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n & \\, & \\, & 2x & ={330}^{∘}-{120}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n \\\\ 2x & =-{90}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n & \\, & \\, & 2x & ={210}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n \\\\ x & =-{45}^{∘}+{180}^{∘}\\cdot n & \\, & \\, & x & ={105}^{∘}+{180}^{∘}\\cdot n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that $a={105}^{∘}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-330218/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a180dc90-c6b9-577e-9eef-ed60ecafe4e5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-330218"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-19756/selection/3224ab5f6f5fb64621a714f7654c4df06661a69e7edb8f5993dcef1e46ce3dea" :answer/id #uuid "5c638b96-47ee-5f46-bd44-e2c319c9a92c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-19756/selection/cffbb322f8b7f15111a1fed32b4f30c182ebbfb47cf454a453cff91913793354" :answer/id #uuid "2a78bf9c-d026-5c91-a854-d7de279eb858" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{16}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-19756/selection/41a74576debbd77023c8544bb1312a27faaff8cd498a0748fed1b5615823e294" :answer/id #uuid "4a281838-b650-5d7a-81e1-369454da05c3" :answ