\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=-\\frac{3}{8}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-19756/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a180dc90-c6b9-577e-9eef-ed60ecafe4e5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-19756"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-328240/field-1/51b7e71ac415d62fcd6302db1c518c0badce55dda03eceebe662e87a5996a8b4" :answer/id #uuid "99b0beee-b0fa-53d0-a2ce-030d3810209c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "85" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-328240/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "b8fbf220-6b4b-525a-acbd-ef5e1b674642" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-328240/field-1/51b7e71ac415d62fcd6302db1c518c0badce55dda03eceebe662e87a5996a8b4" :answer-field/choices ["q-328240/field-1/51b7e71ac415d62fcd6302db1c518c0badce55dda03eceebe662e87a5996a8b4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-328240" :question/id #uuid "c9437a79-2002-51b0-8bf3-405d6098af03" :question/math-academy-id "q-328240" :question/problem "Consider the following trigonometric equation: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+{50}^{∘})=-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\n$$\n\n  \n\nThe general solution of this equation can be expressed as\n\n$$\nx=a+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n,\\,x={175}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is any integer. Find a possible value of $a$ in the range $({0}^{∘},{90}^{∘}].$\n\n$a=$\n{{field-1}}${}^{∘}$" :question/worked-solution "The general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+{50}^{∘} & ={135}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n, & \\, & \\, & x+{50}^{∘} & ={225}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the two equations above for $x,$ we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={135}^{∘}-{50}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n & \\, & \\, & x & ={225}^{∘}-{50}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n \\\\ x & ={85}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n & \\, & \\, & x & ={175}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that $a={85}^{∘}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-328240/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a180dc90-c6b9-577e-9eef-ed60ecafe4e5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-328240"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-328237/field-1/897ce4c7911f99b265ba23f864c4eaa9aec53942cbd2bbe07376f6b49ce12837" :answer/id #uuid "8f74355d-ff69-5e27-a515-2a5fd8f55d67" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "95" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-328237/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "da6c17b7-c1e2-563b-aa55-a2edef18d467" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-328237/field-1/897ce4c7911f99b265ba23f864c4eaa9aec53942cbd2bbe07376f6b49ce12837" :answer-field/choices ["q-328237/field-1/897ce4c7911f99b265ba23f864c4eaa9aec53942cbd2bbe07376f6b49ce12837"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-328237" :question/id #uuid "3ff48e49-1d81-5ee1-b181-e43dce476999" :question/math-academy-id "q-328237" :question/problem "Consider the following trigonometric equation: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+{125}^{∘})=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\n$$\n\n  \n\nThe general solution of this equation can be expressed as\n\n$$\nx=-{40}^{∘}+{180}^{∘}\\cdot n,\\,x=a+{180}^{∘}\\cdot n,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is any integer. Find a possible value of $a$ in the range $[{0}^{∘},{180}^{∘}).$\n\n$a=$\n{{field-1}}${}^{∘}$" :question/worked-solution "The general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+{125}^{∘} & ={45}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n, & \\, & \\, & 2x+{125}^{∘} & ={315}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the two equations above for $x,$ we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x & ={45}^{∘}-{125}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n & \\, & \\, & 2x & ={315}^{∘}-{125}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n \\\\ 2x & =-{80}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n & \\, & \\, & 2x & ={190}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n \\\\ x & =-{40}^{∘}+{180}^{∘}\\cdot n & \\, & \\, & x & ={95}^{∘}+{180}^{∘}\\cdot n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that $a={95}^{∘}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-328237/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a180dc90-c6b9-577e-9eef-ed60ecafe4e5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-328237"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-42800/selection/aa640bdf1bd5b2b15c3dbfe770f68b41d304d610e4d1af786c1f1372fe3dc48f" :answer/id #uuid "f97fbfa3-2919-5c1f-9f3e-cfe50f54bc39" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-42800/selection/29f1bd004b0e742e8153de2e3a77945bac059aed56c8ead2bc0011a45597d328" :answer/id #uuid "6181be44-4b76-5745-86b9-4ac35f4a7823" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{12}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-42800/selection/f130bed8d6b969dc9fba227edf269de52d0a72731cb4fb925914e1521739f418" :answer/id #uuid "fd778905-d531-5c6c-8fec-23c7b781c07e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{24}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-42800/selection/067f8394ee42d8135073fd0c196cd07b15b62bf00b668a6dd30a825b7176ad3f" :answer/id #uuid "eee3248c-0075-5099-b617-4bce0d6f5717" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{10}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-42800/selection/71b1db0b2a675655ec27a2d2ceef2e86712a68eb78548232215378e0a354fb4c" :answer/id #uuid "bb2076ec-aa51-5038-9de8-b30d4b8869a6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-42800/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6f4d6feb-9da3-537c-9629-0de0aafa5857" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-42800/selection/29f1bd004b0e742e8153de2e3a77945bac059aed56c8ead2bc0011a45597d328" :answer-field/choices ["q-42800/selection/aa640bdf1bd5b2b15c3dbfe770f68b41d304d610e4d1af786c1f1372fe3dc48f" "q-42800/selection/29f1bd004b0e742e8153de2e3a77945bac059aed56c8ead2bc0011a45597d328" "q-42800/selection/f130bed8d6b969dc9fba227edf269de52d0a72731cb4fb925914e1521739f418" "q-42800/selection/067f8394ee42d8135073fd0c196cd07b15b62bf00b668a6dd30a825b7176ad3f" "q-42800/selection/71b1db0b2a675655ec27a2d2ceef2e86712a68eb78548232215378e0a354fb4c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-42800" :question/id #uuid "336b79c5-18db-552d-b951-bcb2a0206897" :question/math-academy-id "q-42800" :question/problem "Consider the following trigonometric equation: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}-\\frac{\\pi }{8})=-\\sqrt{3}\n$$\n\nThe general solution of this equation can be expressed as \n\n$$\nx=a\\pi +2n\\pi ,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is any integer. Which of the following could be the value of $a?$" :question/worked-solution "The given equation is equivalent to \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}-\\frac{\\pi }{8})=-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}.\n$$\n\nSo, the general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{2}-\\frac{\\pi }{8} & =-\\frac{\\pi }{6}+n\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the above equation for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{2} & =\\frac{\\pi }{8}-\\frac{\\pi }{6}+n\\pi  \\\\ \\frac{x}{2} & =-\\frac{\\pi }{24}+n\\pi  \\\\ x & =-\\frac{\\pi }{12}+2n\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that $a=-\\frac{1}{12}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-42800/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "97786302-e865-5581-b08e-8da7c6b7a01b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-42800"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-328425/field-1/66dedd51c696580d351ab6a45c1c63cb495081ccf219c3c3c62f1d90fbeb5a49" :answer/id #uuid "5e6e6c86-19b5-5ec4-8709-587ec4eda889" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "15" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-328425/field-1/a4c8bdda186d0d425e9963bf17967cd5e356d934f319fa58135b8f8cf8a589f8" :answer/id #uuid "b94c29a2-a684-585b-9732-b32947eaf8ef" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "30" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-328425/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "9ff6a574-745c-5e34-989b-ef8731d3e884" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-328425/field-1/66dedd51c696580d351ab6a45c1c63cb495081ccf219c3c3c62f1d90fbeb5a49" :answer-field/choices ["q-328425/field-1/66dedd51c696580d351ab6a45c1c63cb495081ccf219c3c3c62f1d90fbeb5a49" "q-328425/field-1/a4c8bdda186d0d425e9963bf17967cd5e356d934f319fa58135b8f8cf8a589f8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-328425" :question/id #uuid "ba4307cd-dbfa-5f5c-927a-c736896cca91" :question/math-academy-id "q-328425" :question/problem "Consider the following trigonometric equation: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cot}⁡(4x+{30}^{∘})=0\n$$\n\nThe general solution of this equation can be expressed as \n\n$$\nx=a+n\\cdot {45}^{∘},\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is any integer. Find a possible value of $a$ in the range $[{0}^{∘},{45}^{∘}).$\n\n$a=$\n{{field-1}}${}^{∘}$" :question/worked-solution "The given equation is equivalent to \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x+{30}^{∘})=0.\n$$\n\nSo, the general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x+{30}^{∘} & ={90}^{∘}+n\\cdot {180}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the above equation for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x & ={90}^{∘}-{30}^{∘}+n\\cdot {180}^{∘} \\\\ 4x & ={60}^{∘}+n\\cdot {180}^{∘} \\\\ x & ={15}^{∘}+n\\cdot {45}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that $a={15}^{∘}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-328425/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "97786302-e865-5581-b08e-8da7c6b7a01b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-328425"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-121064/selection/5ab3573096b30d3c5d3c378e667364cbb062f921e9b1002441e594f0774a669d" :answer/id #uuid "07130973-fe51-567d-aefd-749ce7d301d2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/i