e expressed as \n\n$$\nx=a\\pi +\\frac{n\\pi }{3},\n$$\n\n \nwhere $n$ is any integer. What could be the value of $a?$" :question/worked-solution "The general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x & =-\\frac{\\pi }{3}+n\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the above equation for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x & =-\\frac{\\pi }{3}+n\\pi  \\\\ x & =-\\frac{\\pi }{9}+\\frac{n\\pi }{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that $a=-\\frac{1}{9}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-121064/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "97786302-e865-5581-b08e-8da7c6b7a01b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-121064"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-328250/field-1/7838a4292fc4d1be267381fac8172598f984073c76c5a33cd29bf9790790a9cb" :answer/id #uuid "4a533e69-4803-510e-a5a4-f64179585cb2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "37.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-328250/field-1/ca566c3861ad95266b92d3d8e36c85c39daf1d1780cc1bf826ae0ac7accce583" :answer/id #uuid "59c4bb4b-5d88-561a-b814-a21b05f8d3a3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "45" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-328250/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "ba0bdefe-45bc-59ec-a82c-9194b0659243" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-328250/field-1/7838a4292fc4d1be267381fac8172598f984073c76c5a33cd29bf9790790a9cb" :answer-field/choices ["q-328250/field-1/7838a4292fc4d1be267381fac8172598f984073c76c5a33cd29bf9790790a9cb" "q-328250/field-1/ca566c3861ad95266b92d3d8e36c85c39daf1d1780cc1bf826ae0ac7accce583"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-328250" :question/id #uuid "c86bceb5-09a7-500b-b424-00e8e45afd90" :question/math-academy-id "q-328250" :question/problem "Consider the following trigonometric equation: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x-{30}^{∘})=1\n$$\n\nThe general solution of this equation can be expressed as \n\n$$\nx=a+n\\cdot {90}^{∘},\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere $n$ is any integer. Find a possible value $a$ in the range $[{0}^{∘},{90}^{∘}).$\n\n$a=$\n{{field-1}}${}^{∘}$" :question/worked-solution "The general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-{30}^{∘} & ={45}^{∘}+n\\cdot {180}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the above equation for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x & ={45}^{∘}+{30}^{∘}+n\\cdot {180}^{∘} \\\\ 2x & ={75}^{∘}+n\\cdot {180}^{∘} \\\\ x & ={37.5}^{∘}+n\\cdot {90}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that $a=37.5.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-328250/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "97786302-e865-5581-b08e-8da7c6b7a01b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-328250"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-328434/field-1/9e11fa4df3725c69efaf2fb0a82d90e47a4519d002f721e23606c3d6290fb02c" :answer/id #uuid "92601dc4-0050-5a19-b9f0-fc73ccb31553" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-328434/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "8b5e88a9-c874-5ca0-b627-764f9f21763b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-328434/field-1/9e11fa4df3725c69efaf2fb0a82d90e47a4519d002f721e23606c3d6290fb02c" :answer-field/choices ["q-328434/field-1/9e11fa4df3725c69efaf2fb0a82d90e47a4519d002f721e23606c3d6290fb02c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-328434" :question/id #uuid "49b2ee85-1a6f-5f10-affa-73f92f4121c4" :question/math-academy-id "q-328434" :question/problem "Consider the following trigonometric equation: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}-\\frac{\\pi }{3})=-1\n$$\n\nThe general solution of this equation can be expressed as \n\n$$\nx=a\\pi +2n\\pi ,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is any integer. Find a possible value of $a$ in the range $[0,2).$\n\n$a=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The given equation is equivalent to \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}-\\frac{\\pi }{3})=-1.\n$$\n\nSo, the general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{2}-\\frac{\\pi }{3} & =-\\frac{\\pi }{4}+n\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the above equation for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{2} & =\\frac{\\pi }{3}-\\frac{\\pi }{4}+n\\pi  \\\\ \\frac{x}{2} & =\\frac{\\pi }{12}+n\\pi  \\\\ x & =\\frac{\\pi }{6}+2n\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that $a=\\frac{1}{6}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-328434/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "97786302-e865-5581-b08e-8da7c6b7a01b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-328434"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-328452/field-1/9700accffa78065d8053126335d2ac4e2336d0d88c76df9e6a237030f752585a" :answer/id #uuid "f8184fa4-8e05-5b4d-a609-a70179503aca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-328452/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "0572e39f-2d80-5b82-869f-695d5035edc6" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-328452/field-1/9700accffa78065d8053126335d2ac4e2336d0d88c76df9e6a237030f752585a" :answer-field/choices ["q-328452/field-1/9700accffa78065d8053126335d2ac4e2336d0d88c76df9e6a237030f752585a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-328452" :question/id #uuid "67ae8131-8848-5415-a2f6-cec00ad3c84e" :question/math-academy-id "q-328452" :question/problem "Consider the following trigonometric equation:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sec}⁡(3x)=-2\n$$\n\nThe general solution of this equation is\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{2\\pi }{9}+\\frac{2\\pi n}{3},\\,x=a\\pi +\\frac{2\\pi n}{3},\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is any integer. Find a possible value of $a$ in the range $[0,\\frac{2}{3}).$\n\n$a=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, note that the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)=-\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n3x=\\frac{2\\pi }{3}+2\\pi n,\\,3x=\\frac{4\\pi }{3}+2\\pi n.\n$$\n\nSolving the two equations above for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x & =\\frac{2\\pi }{3}+2\\pi n, & \\,3x & =\\frac{4\\pi }{3}+2\\pi n \\\\ x & =\\frac{2\\pi }{9}+\\frac{2\\pi n}{3}, & \\,x & =\\frac{4\\pi }{9}+\\frac{2\\pi n}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have that $a=\\frac{4}{9}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-328452/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3ea83062-5744-52ef-9b3e-f9805ed092fb"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-328452"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-42788"] :question/problem "Consider the following trigonometric equation:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{x}{4}+{20}^{∘})=2.\n$$\n\nThe general solution of this equation is\n\n$$\nx={a}^{∘}+1\\,{440}^{∘}\\cdot n,\\,x=1\\,{120}^{∘}+1\\,{440}^{∘}\\cdot n,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is any integer. Which of the following could be the value of $a?$" :question/worked-solution "First, note that the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{4}+{20}^{∘})=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\frac{x}{4}+{20}^{∘}={60}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n,\\,\\frac{x}{4}+{20}^{∘}={300}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n.\n$$\n\nSolving the two equations above for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{4}=-{20}^{∘}+{60}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n, & \\,\\frac{x}{4}=-{20}^{∘}+{300}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n \\\\ \\frac{x}{4}={40}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n, & \\,\\frac{x}{4}={280}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n \\\\ x={160}^{∘}+1\\,{440}^{∘}\\cdot n, & \\,x=1\\,{120}^{∘}+1\\,{440}^{∘}\\cdot n.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have that $a=160.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-121076/selection/98cd92164dc5a108f65f30de322938d029ae78aa0e7fd19c5839ede6270aefa9" :answer/id #uuid "0096e992-63ab-5731-ab9a-4ae0e332eeb2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7\\pi }{30}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121076/selection/d62732e72e17b0393290bd9e548ef368f6b7424bded817d038b07db5bf5fcb98" :answer/id #uuid "4e899ce5-e583-53a1-827e-7429bf319bfc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121076/selection/64c71371d488b2cb9e911696217ada7d2c48e37d45a038655a5f6dc703e9f6fc" :answer/id #uuid "2df6e8df-3e7e-50d4-9019-054f1b4765b3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{6\\pi }{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121076/selection/c2db034559420b121b995a068bdfea5fe16f2b700d9ebe187704e3ea55c1239e" :answer/id #uuid "d3932372-9171-5f70-8c8f-316868ba95c4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7\\pi }{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121076/selection/49038b61ea067d6dd93788348f33b8daf64ac00ab39a6be298018d209f477567" :answer/id #uuid "f531d1ab-646b-50c9-9dd6-64907eef1f71" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5\\pi }{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121076/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "ecd6b3ae-8526-5334-a9aa-490618f27f79" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-121076/selection/98cd92164dc5a108f65f30de322938d029ae78aa0e7fd19c5839ede6270aefa9" :answer-field/choices ["q-121076/selection/98cd92164dc5a108f65f30de322938d029ae78aa0e7fd19c5839ede6270aefa9" "q-121076/selection/d62732e72e17b0393290bd9e548ef368f6b7424bded817d038b07db5bf5fcb98" "q-121076/selection/64c71371d488b2cb9e911696217ada7d2c48e37d45a038655a5f6dc703e9f6fc" "q-121076/selection/c2db034559420b121b995a068bdfea5fe16f2b700d9ebe187704e3ea55c1239e" "q-121076/selection/49038b61ea067d6dd93788348f33b8daf64ac00ab39a6be298018d209f477567"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-121076" :question/id #uuid "9a968c79-5a9b-586d-b119-90ef0b955726" :question/math-academy-id "q-121076" :question/problem "Consider the following trigonometric equation:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sec}⁡(5x)=-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}\n$$\n\nThe general solution of this equation is\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\frac{2\\pi n}{5},\\,x=a+\\frac{2\\pi n}{5},\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is any integer. Which of the following could be the value of $a?$" :question/worked-solution "First, note that the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)=-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n5x=\\frac{5\\pi }{6}+2\\pi n,\\,5x=\\frac{7\\pi }{6}+2\\pi n.\n$$\n\nSolving the two equations above for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x & =\\frac{5\\pi }{6}+2\\pi n, & \\,5x & =\\frac{7\\pi }{6}+2\\pi n \\\\ x & =\\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\frac{2\\pi n}{5}, & \\,x & =\\frac{7\\pi }{30}+\\frac{2\\pi n}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have that $a=\\frac{7\\pi }{30}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-121076/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3ea83062-5744-52ef-9b3e-f9805ed092fb"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-121076"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-42789"] :question/problem "Consider the following trigonometric  equation:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{csc}⁡2x=-2\n$$\n\nThe general solution of this equation can be expressed as \n\n$$\nx=a+\\pi n,\\,x=\\frac{11\\pi }{12}+\\pi n,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is any integer. Which of the following could be the value of $a?$" :question/worked-solution "First, note that the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x=-\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n2x=\\frac{7\\pi }{6}+2n\\pi ,\\,x=\\frac{11\\pi }{6}+2\\pi n.\n$$\n\nSolving the two equations above for $x,$ we get:\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{7\\pi }{12}+n\\pi ,\\,x=\\frac{11\\pi }{12}+n\\pi \\,\\,\n$$\n\nSo, we have that $a=\\frac{7\\pi }{12}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-121068/selection/fa2764e4d443b0fd1a8b9b79f38b985d2b576f72681c3b867c06cfeb24c839e4" :answer/id #uuid "b7d32859-686c-5df3-a522-9dcec0ca38e0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "360" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121068/selection/a59e10e9ca0b8a69d2b8425f1c9930ee0733ea061a1d6430398562813d750649" :answer/id #uuid "6fa20bed-c0ee-5160-9cb3-f04fe3d0f927" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "120" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121068/selection/557015e94af5fa4bd02ae0ff131d8572cb165f5648829317508c9b9e01215bfe" :answer/id #uuid "d9dfaab9-8548-5173-9971-c29f6d1de9f0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "240" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121068/selection/e792eba67a521531d68e5f67786d5b3cea0fc3869014543152be243f2639fb08" :answer/id #uuid "3a481257-67ca-5aba-811f-7131c8a0cea5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "300" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121068/selection/1ad763bfa28dd8bf929699f6c31cff536336c19979c6baa533b7a886875a37b7" :answer/id #uuid "1f63b9c6-8b22-55d3-9f1c-655f92571064" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "270" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121068/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "2d88ec9b-a5c6-5f52-b55a-3f23e591225c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-121068/selection/557015e94af5fa4bd02ae0ff131d8572cb165f5648829317508c9b9e01215bfe" :answer-field/choices ["q-121068/selection/fa2764e4d443b0fd1a8b9b79f38b985d2b576f72681c3b867c06cfeb24c839e4" "q-121068/selection/a59e10e9ca0b8a69d2b8425f1c9930ee0733ea061a1d6430398562813d750649" "q-121068/selection/557015e94af5fa4bd02ae0ff131d8572cb165f5648829317508c9b9e01215bfe" "q-121068/selection/e792eba67a521531d68e5f67786d5b3cea0fc3869014543152be243f2639fb08" "q-121068/selection/1ad763bfa28dd8bf929699f6c31cff536336c19979c6baa533b7a886875a37b7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-121068" :question/id #uuid "e2a4d635-4370-5450-961f-de86ce3806b8" :question/math-academy-id "q-121068" :question/problem "Consider the following trigonometric equation:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})=-2.\n$$\n\nThe general solution of this equation is\n\n$$\nx={a}^{∘}+{720}^{∘}\\cdot n,\\,x={480}^{∘}+{720}^{∘}\\cdot n,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is any integer. Which of the following could be the value of $a?$" :question/worked-solution "First, note that the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})=-\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\frac{x}{2}={120}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n,\\,\\frac{x}{2}={240}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n.\n$$\n\nSolving the two equations above for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{2} & ={120}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n, & \\,\\frac{x}{2} & ={240}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n \\\\ x & ={240}^{∘}+{720}^{∘}\\cdot n, & \\,x & ={480}^{∘}+{720}^{∘}\\cdot n.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have that $a=240.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-121068/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3ea83062-5744-52ef-9b3e-f9805ed092fb"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-121068"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-3779"] :question/problem "Find the general solution of the following trigonometric equation: \n\n$$\n\\sin{\\left(4x-90^\\circ\\right)} = -\\dfrac{1}{2}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x-{90}^{∘} & =-{30}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}n, & \\, & \\, & 4x-{90}^{∘} & =-{150}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}n.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the two equations above for $x,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x & ={90}^{∘}-{30}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}n & \\, & \\, & 4x & ={90}^{∘}-{150}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}n \\\\ 4x & ={60}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}n & \\, & \\, & 4x & =-{60}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}n \\\\ x & ={15}^{∘}+{90}^{∘}n & \\, & \\, & x & =-{15}^{∘}+{90}^{∘}n\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-8659"] :question/problem "Find the general solution of the following trigonometric equation:\n\n$$\n\\cos \\left(6x + 75^\\circ \\right) = -\\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6x+{75}^{∘} & ={135}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘}, & \\, & \\, & 6x+{75}^{∘} & ={225}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the two equations above for $x,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6x & ={60}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘} & \\, & \\, & 6x & ={150}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘} \\\\ x & ={10}^{∘}+n\\cdot {60}^{∘} & \\, & \\, & x & ={25}^{∘}+n\\cdot {60}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-3780"] :question/problem "Find the general solution of the following trigonometric equation:\n\n$$\n\\tan\\left(2x - \\dfrac{\\pi}{4} \\right) =  -1\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-\\frac{\\pi }{4} & =-\\frac{\\pi }{4}+n\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the above equation for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x & =n\\pi  \\\\ x & =\\frac{n\\pi }{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-3781"] :question/problem "Find the general solution of the following trigonometric equation:\n\n$$\n\\sec\\left(2x + \\dfrac{\\pi}{2}\\right) = \\sqrt{2}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, note that the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\cos\\left(2x + \\dfrac{\\pi}{2}\\right) = \\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n2x + \\dfrac{\\pi}{2} = \\dfrac{\\pi}{4} + 2\\pi n, \\qquad\\qquad 2x + \\dfrac{\\pi}{2} = \\dfrac{7\\pi}{4} + 2\\pi n.\n$$\n\nSolving the two equations above for $x,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x=-\\frac{\\pi }{2}+\\frac{\\pi }{4}+2\\pi n, & \\, & \\, & 2x=-\\frac{\\pi }{2}+\\frac{7\\pi }{4}+2\\pi n \\\\ 2x=-\\frac{\\pi }{4}+2\\pi n, & \\, & \\, & 2x=\\frac{5\\pi }{4}+2\\pi n \\\\ x=-\\frac{\\pi }{8}+\\pi n, & \\, & \\, & x=\\frac{5\\pi }{8}+\\pi n\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
